  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 13 files required for this dependency-graph analysis, covering:\n\n1. **Log4j2 bridge/detection modules** (`log4j-to-slf4j/pom.xml`, `log4j-slf4j-impl/pom.xml`, `log4j-slf4j2-impl/pom.xml`, `log4j-api/pom.xml`, root `pom.xml`) \u2014 shows the module split: `log4j-to-slf4j` (Log4j2 API \u2192 routes to SLF4J), vs `log4j-slf4j-impl`/`log4j-slf4j2-impl` (SLF4J API \u2192 routes to Log4j2 Core), the SLF4J 1.x/2.x split, and the multi-module parent structure.\n2. **Spring Boot's logging auto-configuration/detection core** (`LoggingSystem.java`, `LoggingSystemFactory.java`, `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java`, `LoggingApplicationListener.java`, `spring.factories`) \u2014 the `spring.factories`-driven `LoggingSystemFactory` SPI that detects which logging implementation is on the classpath (`Log4jContextFactory` presence check) and wires it via `ApplicationStartingEvent`.\n3. **The cross-repo bridge point** (`Log4j2SpringBootLoggingSystem.java` + its test in the log4j2 repo) \u2014 Log4j2 ships its own `LoggingSystemFactory` override (`@Order(0)`, highest precedence) that extends Spring Boot's `Log4J2LoggingSystem` to support Spring Cloud Config, demonstrating the extension/override chain between the two repos.\n4. Test files for both to confirm detection-logic behavior under classpath variations.",
